    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d355">

                <pb facs="0373" n="367" xml:id="pg367"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/24142b: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Dakar
                        (Flexer)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-09-02T22:00:00-04:00">September 2,
                            1942—10 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>86. For your strictly confidential information the Embassy at Vichy reports that
                    it has been informed that Laval and Abetz<anchor n="46" xml:id="d355-f1"/> held
                    a conference at Nevers on August 27 to discuss Dakar. It appears that previously
                    the Germans had sought permission to send a squadron of Stukas to Dakar, which
                    threatened to provoke the resignation of Boisson, who is thought to have been
                    willing to accept the Stukas but not German pilots. The Embassy has been
                    informed that Boisson recently forwarded his resignation to the Marshal<anchor
                        n="47" xml:id="d355-f2"/> through Barrau but that the Marshal would not
                    accept it on the grounds that the proposed German mission was only of a
                    temporary character.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d355-f1" n="46" xml:id="d355-f1-content">
                <p>Otto Abetz, German Ambassador in Paris.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d355-f2" n="47" xml:id="d355-f2-content">
                <p>Marshal Henri Philippe Pétain, French Chief of State.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
